projects.description:
This high-level conference on Sustainable Ocean Economy and Climate Change Adaptation organized by the Governments of Viet Nam and Norway and UNDP in hybrid format in Hanoi, Viet Nam brings together leaders, practitioners, scientists, experts, private sector and civil society together  to: 
1. Discuss the key opportunities to promote sustainable utilization of ocean resources as well as key challenges posed by the Covid-19 crisis, climate change and environmental pollution including the Global Agreement on Plastic Pollution Ocean; 
2. Identify opportunities to accelerate actions to protect ocean ecosystems for economic development and enhance the adaptation and resilience of vulnerable countries and communities;
3. Share experiences, best practices and research results, to enhance knowledge of successful sustainable ocean economy, climate change adaption strategies and actions; and
4. Encourage networking of South-South and South-North collaboration, foster cooperation and develop synergies between initiatives. 
Key Conference results and recommended priority actions will be set out in a Co-Chairs' Joint Statement.
